  "releaseNotes": "2.0.1 — Fix: request URLs are now built with a joinUrl() helper instead of\n      raw string concatenation, so a base URL configured with a trailing slash combined with an\n      endpoint path starting with a leading slash (common with OpenAPI-imported paths) no longer\n      produces a doubled // in the constructed request URL. No public API changes. See CHANGELOG.md\n      for full history.",
